  "preamble": "Denasalization and lowering of the nasalized front mid vowel [ẽ] to the open vowel [a]. In East Slavic, Proto-Slavic *ę lost its nasality and became [a], leaving the preceding consonant palatalized, as in Russian мясо 'meat' and мята 'mint'.",
